## Env — read only via `@/libs/env`

- Never read `process.env` directly. Import `env` from
  `@/libs/env` (which re-exports from `./env`).
- Schema: `src/libs/env/env.ts`. Add new vars there with a Zod schema.
  Server vars in the `server` block; `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` in `client`.
- `runtimeEnv` MUST list every var (tsc strict — `createEnv` errors
  on missing entries).
- `skipValidation: process.env.SKIP_ENV_VALIDATION === 'true'` exists
  for build-time tooling; do not set it in app code.
- The shared `@shadhil/auth` package depends on the same `BETTER_AUTH_*`,
  `JWT_*`, `DIRECT_DATABASE_URL` keys. Both apps must agree or
  `pnpm dev` will fail at boot — see `apps/web/.env` for the source.

## Providers — single tree in `src/providers/providers.tsx`

Current order (matters for context inheritance):

1. `NextThemeProvider` — `next-themes` wrapper, SSR-safe, drives
   `.dark` on `<html>`. Use this, **not** the homegrown `ThemeProvider`
   from `@paalstack/react-ui` — that one calls `localStorage.getItem`
   in a `useState` initializer and crashes SSR.
2. `QueryProvider` — `QueryClientProvider` over the singleton from
   `@/libs/query-client` (5 min `staleTime` / `gcTime`, no retries,
   focus-refetch in production only).
3. `children`.

`<Toaster />` is imported but not yet mounted — that's a known TODO
from Phase 1. When you wire it, mount it inside `Providers` (theme
context is needed for sonner to re-skin on toggle).

## Dynamic rendering for theme persistence

The `Providers` subtree reads `localStorage` on mount (theme
persistence via `next-themes`). Next 16's static prerender chokes on
that. Any page that renders inside `Providers` must opt out:

```tsx
export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic';
```

See `src/app/page.tsx` and `src/app/not-found.tsx`. Apply the same to
every new page until we remove the theme-provider localStorage read.

## Route handlers

```tsx
// src/app/api/<name>/route.ts
export const GET = () => Response.json({ ok: true });
export const POST = async (req: Request) => { /* ... */ };
```

- Better-auth lives at `src/app/api/auth/[...all]/route.ts` via
  `toNextJsHandler(auth.handler)` from `better-auth/next-js`. The
  `auth` instance is re-exported from `@shadhil/auth` via
  `src/lib/auth.ts` — both apps share the same instance.
- `/api/health` is the canonical liveness probe — extend, don't
  duplicate.
- No `withApiErrorHandling` / `apiSuccess` / typed `AppError*` wrapper
  exists yet in apps/web. The Nest backend has one
  (`apps/backend/src/common/error/`); **don't** assume Next route
  handlers inherit it. Until the wrapper lands here, throw
  `HttpError` from `@paalstack/react-ui/lib` or return `Response.json(
  { error }, { status })` directly.

## Env-aware backend calls

`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` points at the Nest backend (default
`http://localhost:8080`). Use the `httpClient` from
`@paalstack/react-ui/lib` or your own axios/fetch — but always go
through the env var, never hardcode `localhost`.

