## Do Not

- Author library components here. This is a consumer app — push changes
  to `paalstack-react-ui` upstream.
- Duplicate Button/Input/Dialog/Table/Form/Select/Checkbox or the common
  hooks the library already provides.
- Write new `useMediaQuery`, `useLocalStorage`, `useDisclosure` —
  `@paalstack/react-hooks` covers them.
- Import the `@paalstack/react-icons` root barrel or install icon
  packages directly.
- Use raw hex colors when semantic tokens exist.
- Use native HTML elements in JSX.
- Read `process.env` directly — use `env` from `@/libs/env`.
- Use the homegrown `ThemeProvider` from `@paalstack/react-ui` — it
  crashes SSR. Use `NextThemeProvider`.
- Skip `export const dynamic = 'force-dynamic'` on pages wrapped by
  `Providers`.
- Create `src/apis/`, `src/hooks/queries/`, `src/hooks/mutations/`,
  `src/schemas/`, `src/features/`, `src/stores/`, `src/types/`,
  `src/utils/`, `src/components/ui/`, `src/components/shared/`,
  `src/libs/axios/`, `src/libs/error/`, or `src/libs/logger/`
  directories until the first feature actually needs them. Update
  this rule when you do.

